<p>The United States will withdraw about 5,000 troops from Germany over the next six to 12 months, the Pentagon said Friday, after President Trump publicly threatened to reduce forces stationed in the NATO ally. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth ordered the drawdown, and Pentagon spokesman Sean Parnell said it followed a review of the Defense Department&#x27;s force posture in Europe and reflected “theater requirements and conditions on the ground”. The announcement followed a dispute between President Trump and German Chancellor Friedrich Merz over the U.S. war with Iran, after Merz said Iran&#x27;s leadership was humiliating Washington in talks and questioned the U.S. exit strategy. President Trump later said Washington was studying a possible reduction in U.S. troops in Germany and publicly criticized Merz. Germany hosts more than 35,000 U.S. service members, the largest American deployment in Europe.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/gwON0dn6ZR3hKLuuuSYK9nl175OoKKzD6dvlJZRzFmUAvm6a1NMXntmV0lbJOMxQbRrMve9aO3t5_hDR03udzQRu5AtwuxtvNdkkd8xa1E_zND9Um8kL_sNkA8KOlz_CjwNxWfJFuuoHTU2aJK9yAiE6lBNUDnaWk3dLtv_KFmPFf4L8KCTYhPY_xvcw2WnYNmOx7o0MxEOnVqndGW5lVkh215T-rv9-Z_mw4w4xERyheQ3Iw5xQwdRqGBuWFdKaiZoexFBoIPVfjsS62Q' alt='U.S. Army soldiers train at the Hohenfels Training Area in Hohenfels, Germany.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Deployment scale: Boston.com reported that the departing contingent equals about 14% of the 36,000 U.S. service members stationed there, while Politico said roughly 33,000 troops would remain after the drawdown.</li><li>Headquarters footprint: Germany hosts U.S. European Command and U.S. Africa Command, according to Politico.</li><li>European pressure: President Trump also said he would probably consider reductions in Italy and Spain, while criticizing NATO allies he said had not supported U.S. efforts related to the Strait of Hormuz.</li><li>Oil backdrop: Euronews said the U.S.-Israeli war on Iran had upended the Middle East and contributed to a global oil price crisis.</li></ul><blockquote>We expect the withdrawal to be completed over the next six to twelve months. - Sean Parnell</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pentagon official: A senior Pentagon official, speaking anonymously, described recent German remarks as “unhelpful and inappropriate” and said the president was responding to statements that undermined cooperation. (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/us-to-withdraw-5000-troops-from-germany-amid-growing-rift-with-europe-549129/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li><li>President Trump: President Trump criticized Merz after the German chancellor&#x27;s comments on Iran, writing that Merz “thinks it’s OK for Iran to have a Nuclear Weapon. He doesn’t know what he’s talking about!”. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1996900/us-to-withdraw-about-5000-troops-from-germany'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-withdrawing-5000-troops-from-germany-us-officials-say/article70930666.ece'>U.S. withdrawing 5,000 troops from Germany, U.S. officials say</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3352198/us-withdraw-5000-troops-germany-fulfilling-trump-threat'>US to withdraw 5,000 troops from Germany, fulfilling Trump threat</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/4cabedc3-0119-4c3f-9867-094b7e1398f6'>US to withdraw 5,000 troops from Germany in dispute over Iran conflict</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/us-withdrawing-5000-troops-from-germany-us-officials-say'>US withdrawing 5,000 troops from Germany, US officials say</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/1/us-said-to-be-withdrawing-5000-troops-from-germany-over-iran-war-spat'>US said to be withdrawing 5,000 troops from Germany over Iran war spat</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-germany-5000-troops/'>Trump admin